## Lore

The Ganka are giant plant D-Bees from a world that is mostly tropical
jungle, and they turned up on Rifts Earth only about twenty years ago. They
are few in number and keep to warm, wet country like the Southeast.

A Ganka is a thick, sinewy trunk topped by a bulbous head with an enormous
mouth, big enough to swallow a large dog or a small person whole. Three or
four thick vine-tentacles serve as arms, and a mass of small root-tentacles
carries it along the ground and across swampy, overgrown water. It has no
eyes, ears or nose: it smells and senses heat through receptors in its
mouth and feels sound and movement through fine hairs all over its body.
It cannot read or see colors, but in close quarters its reactions are
nearly as fast as a Juicer''s.

Ganka are friendly, joking, game-loving and fond of rough play, and seem
unaware of how alarming they look or how bad their manners are. They eat
only raw meat, preferring giant insects such as Xiticix and Drizzit, and
take a blunt might-makes-right view of life: death is natural, so they
rarely seek revenge. Some evil Ganka see everyone as potential food, and
even good ones regard insect people as edible.

## GM Notes

Also known as Killer Ganka and Flytrap People. Size 7-9 feet (2.1 to 2.7 m),
mouth 3-4 feet (0.9 to 1.2 m) wide. Weight 200 to 300 pounds (90 to 135 kg).
Life span 2D4+50 years; mature in 1D4+1 years. Females bear a single seed
pod that releases 4D6 young after 11 months; the young hide for 2-5 years
while they grow.

A regrown (resurrected) Ganka is not vengeful, but may retaliate against
its killer in petty ways: theft, cheating, framing or reporting them.

Habitat: hot, moist environments, chiefly in and around Dinosaur Swamp,
with a few in Mexico and South America; can live along temperate streams
and marshes but rarely do. Slave market value: sold in lots of 100 for
3D6x20,000 credits.

Allies: none as such, though they enjoy other plant D-Bees such as the
Cactus People. Enemies: Xiticix are a buffet; they hunt and eat other
intelligent insect D-Bees and mutants as well.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ganka');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ganka';

